-- טבלת המרה לשכר מורים קיימים בדרגת 'בלתי מוסמך' (קוד דירוג 106), מעודכנת החל מיום 1.9.2016: the conversion
-- table of an existing teacher of the uncertified rank (בלתי מוסמך) (rating code 106) from 1.9.2016, as the
-- conditions-of-service portal publishes it. It is annex א'7 of the
-- September 2016 agreement (30.9.2016), whose §5(א) makes annexes א'1–א'7
-- the combined-salary tables from that day and which the corpus holds
-- without its annexes: the agreement takes each cell as a named input
-- (imported). A conversion table is the salary table with the intermediate
-- grades, "for the conversion only" (the base agreement's §46(א)).
--
-- What the agreement says of it, checked here over every cell: it
-- replaces the table in force on 31.8.2016 (annex א'7 of 1.1.2015,
-- imported) and pays less than that only in grades 6.5–9 (§5(ב)(1)(א)), so
-- every cell to grade 6 is the cell of 1.1.2015 and every cell from grade
-- 6.5 below it. Its steps — 2% and 1% beside the rows,
-- 7.5% to every whole grade, each intermediate grade the mean of its
-- neighbours — are checked against its cells.
--
-- The corpus prints each row's step and seniority in one cell ("2% 2") and
-- the header's "1" over that column; its header also prints grades 3.5
-- and 4 in one cell ("4 3.5") with a blank after it, and the 7.5% of
-- grade 4 one cell to the left, under 3.5. The amounts stand in seventeen
-- columns, grades 1 to 9 by halves, as in the other conversion tables;
-- they are read so, and the eight 7.5% steps as the whole grades 2–9.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `base-agreement-46`
IMPORT `tables-common`
IMPORT `2015-01-01_ofek-hadash_salary-tables_morim`
IMPORT `2016-09-30_ofek-hadash_september-2016-agreement`

§ `טבלת המרה לשכר מורים קיימים בדרגת 'בלתי מוסמך' (קוד דירוג 106), 1.9.2016`

-- The page prints no annex label: the table is annex א'7 by its title, the
-- rating code 106 the September 2016 agreement's last table is for.

-- The table prints under it "טבלה מעודכנת החל מיום 1.9.2016": §5(א)'s
-- determining date (asserted below).
